  "rationale": "Preserves the primary drawdown stress mechanism (depth * occupancy) from parent1, which captures acute price pressure from multi-session drawdowns. Adds a lightweight volatility attenuation from parent2: scaling stress by 1/(1+20d rolling std of daily returns). This reduces false signals during high-volatility periods, a predictive weakness of the raw stress signal. The economic intuition is that drawdowns are more mean-reverting when volatility is low; in high-volatility regimes, price moves are noisier and the stress signal is attenuated.",
